                <div class="azure-notes-content">
                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">Chapter 4 - Microsoft Azure - Storage Accounts


Azure Storage Account is a storage account that is a resource that acts as a container that groups all
the data services from Azure storage (Azure blobs, Azure files, Azure Queues, and Azure Tables).
This helps us manage all of them as a group. The policies we specify while creating the storage
account or making changes after the creation applies to all the services inside the account. Deleting a
storage account deletes all the storage services deployed and the data stored inside it.</pre>
